No visual PASS is claimed until the composition owner is applied, PIE starts, and the resulting same-world PNG is inspected.","createdAt":"2026-09-06T02:53:36Z"},{"author":"organicoverlords","body":"Aspen proof review: the existing post-PlayerStart artifact (SHA fde7b4e8b518a8fa8eaab825ae3803e9157aaec713a81c957c253f381a6e87bb) remains an actual visual REJECT on direct pixel inspection: the frame is readable sky over an effectively black/empty lower field, with no usable lineup. Current main's ring radius is 16000 while TuneShowroomComposition places the start at y=-26000 facing center; treat player-entry framing/distance as the next bounded composition defect, not lighting. No map/source mutation here: the canonical source-lane request failed closed at the current 13/10 lane ceiling, so foreign/dirty state was preserved.","createdAt":"2026-09-06T15:12:17Z"},{"author":"organicoverlords","body":"Quantified the same reviewed frame rather than relying only on the manifest aggregate: sampled top-half mean luma is 67.82, bottom-half mean is only 4.24 (1280x720). The ring's nearest anchor is at y=-16000 (index 0), while PlayerStart is y=-26000, so the first display is ~100m ahead and at most ~9m footprint. That geometry is consistent with the direct visual failure: current outside-in start is too distant/low-readability for this legacy ring. A corrected composition should move the player materially closer to the near ring edge and then require a fresh same-world reviewed PNG before acceptance.","createdAt":"2026-09-06T15:18:07Z"}],"state":"OPEN","title":"Finish ALL_ASSETS_Lineup showroom beauty pass"}
